## Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.12
- MySQL running locally

### Installation

**Step 1 — Create and activate virtual environment**
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\activate

**Step 2 — Install PyTorch CPU build first (must be done before requirements.txt)**
pip install torch==2.2.0+cpu torchaudio==2.2.0+cpu --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

**Step 3 — Install remaining dependencies**
pip install -r requirements.txt

**Step 4 — Set up environment variables**
Copy .env.example to .env and fill in your keys.

### Why torch must be installed separately
torch and torchaudio are not on PyPI with the +cpu build tag. 
Installing via requirements.txt will pull the wrong build and 
cause numpy/torchaudio ABI conflicts with pyannote and speechbrain.
Always install torch first using the PyTorch index URL above.

### Windows (local dev)
pip install torch==2.2.0+cpu torchaudio==2.2.0+cpu --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
pip install -r requirements_windows.txt

### Linux (production)
pip install -r requirements.txt

